## 2. FFmpeg

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Component | FFmpeg (`ffmpeg` CLI binary, and a WebAssembly build of the same sources for the web target) |
| Upstream | <https://ffmpeg.org/> / <https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg> |
| Version | **9.0.2** (git tag `n9.0.2`, vendored as the `third_party/ffmpeg` submodule) |
| License of the *bundled build* | **GPL v3 or later** — because our build passes `--enable-gpl --enable-version3` |
| Relevant texts | [`LICENSES/ffmpeg/COPYING.GPLv3`](LICENSES/ffmpeg/COPYING.GPLv3), [`LICENSES/ffmpeg/LICENSE.md`](LICENSES/ffmpeg/LICENSE.md), [`LICENSES/ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1`](LICENSES/ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1) |

Upstream FFmpeg is LGPL v2.1+ by default; the optional GPL-only parts are activated by
`--enable-gpl`, which makes the resulting binary GPL. We additionally pass `--enable-version3` so
the result is GPL **v3**-or-later — the strictest license FFmpeg can be distributed under while
staying free. `--enable-nonfree` is forbidden in this repository and is checked by the build
scripts (`scripts/ffmpeg/common.sh`).

### Corresponding source

The complete source of the bundled FFmpeg is the contents of the `third_party/ffmpeg` submodule at
commit `n9.0.2`. A recipient of a binary can reproduce it byte-for-byte from:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg.git
git -C FFmpeg checkout n9.0.2
./scripts/ffmpeg/build-<target>.sh    # exact configure flags are printed by the script
```

The build scripts print the full `configure` command line and write it to
`build/ffmpeg/dist/<target>/configure.txt`, so the "preferred form for modification" is fully
specified. No local patches are applied to FFmpeg.

### No external (non-FFmpeg) libraries

The bundled builds currently link **only** FFmpeg's own in-tree implementations (plus, where the
platform provides it, `zlib`). Consequently the only third-party license to honour for the
multimedia stack is FFmpeg's. If an external codec library (x264, x265, libvpx, opus, …) is added
later, it must be added as a submodule **and** registered in this file with its license text placed
in `LICENSES/` — the build contract forbids unlicensed linkage.

## 3. Flutter / Dart / Android / platform SDKs

* Flutter and the Dart SDK — BSD-3-Clause (see the Flutter SDK's `LICENSE`).
* Android SDK / NDK, MSYS2 runtime, MinGW-w64, Emscripten — their own licenses; they are build-time
  toolchains and, apart from MinGW's runtime support already statically linked into the Windows
  `ffmpeg.exe`, they are not redistributed by this project.

## 4. Compliance checklist for distributors

1. Ship `LICENSE`, `NOTICE` and the whole `LICENSES/` directory alongside the application.
2. Provide the corresponding source of this app ("preferred form for modification").
3. Provide the FFmpeg source at tag `n9.0.2` (submodule contents) — a written offer is not enough
   for GPL v3 if you distribute binaries over the network; host the source or point at a mirror you
   control in addition to upstream.
4. Do not modify the bundled binary's build flags to add `--enable-nonfree`.
